---
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro'
import {
	IS_DRAFT,
	OPERATOR,
	TERMS_DATE_LABEL,
	TERMS_VERSION,
	VENUE,
	WEBAPP_HOST,
	WEBSITE_HOST,
	field,
} from '../../legal'

/**
 * Английская оферта в редакции юриста (3 августа 2026).
 *
 * Приоритет по-прежнему за русской версией — так сказано в шапке документа, — но текст
 * здесь уже не перевод: юрист добавил конструкции англо-американского права, которых в
 * русской оферте нет. Расходятся §4 (лицензия на сервис), §6 (лицензия на контент
 * пользователя), §9 (отказ от подразумеваемых гарантий) и §10 (перечень исключаемых
 * убытков). Правки по существу вносятся в обе страницы сразу, иначе разрыв растёт.
 */
---

<Page
	title="Terms of Service — Between Bubbles"
	description="Terms of use for the Between Bubbles service."
	noindex={IS_DRAFT}
	longform
	lang="en"
	alternatePath="/offer"
>
	<p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
	<h1>Terms of Service</h1>
	<p class="version">Last updated: {TERMS_DATE_LABEL.en} · Version: {TERMS_VERSION}</p>

	{
		IS_DRAFT && (
			<div class="notice">
				<p style="margin: 0">
					<strong>Draft.</strong> The text describes the service as it actually works, but
					the rightholder's details have not been confirmed yet and are shown in square
					brackets. Until they are filled in and the text is reviewed by a lawyer, this
					document is not a public offer.
				</p>
			</div>
		)
	}

	<div class="notice">
		<p style="margin: 0">
			This is a translation of the Russian original. In case of any discrepancy between the
			two versions, the <a href="/offer">Russian version</a> prevails.
		</p>
	</div>

	<h2>1. Parties and Subject Matter</h2>
	<p>
		This document is a public offer by {field(OPERATOR.name.en, 'operator name')} (hereinafter —
		the "Rightholder"), addressed to any legally capable adult individual (hereinafter — the
		"User"), to enter into an agreement on the use of the Between Bubbles service on the terms
		set out below.
	</p>
	<p>
		The service is the Between Bubbles web application: a personal wine tasting diary
		available at {WEBSITE_HOST} and {WEBAPP_HOST}. The service is intended for personal,
		non-commercial use: keeping track of what the User has tasted and of their own
		impressions.
	</p>

	<h2>2. Conclusion of the Agreement</h2>
	<p>
		The agreement is considered concluded at the moment the User, during registration, ticks
		the consent checkbox for these terms and the privacy policy and creates an account. The
		service records the date of consent and the document version in effect at that moment.
		No separate signing on paper is required.
	</p>

	<h2>3. Age Restriction</h2>
	<p>
		The service is available only to individuals who have reached 18 years of age. The date of
		birth is requested during registration; providing false information is grounds for
		immediate account suspension. Excessive alcohol consumption is harmful to your health. The
		service does not provide medical advice, does not encourage consumption, and is not an
		advertisement for alcoholic beverages.
	</p>

	<h2>4. License Grant (What the User Receives)</h2>
	<p>
		The Rightholder grants the User a personal, worldwide, non-exclusive, non-transferable, and
		revocable license to use the service for its intended purpose: to keep tasting entries,
		store photos, maintain a personal wine directory, view weekly metrics and statistics,
		export their data, and publish individual entries via a link. This license is not
		transferable to third parties.
	</p>
	<p>
		The service is currently provided free of charge. The set of features may change and
		expand. If paid features appear, their terms will be published in advance as a separate
		document; the export of data already created remains available in any case.
	</p>

	<h2>5. Account Security</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>
			The password and access to the email account are the User's sole responsibility. Actions
			performed under the account are considered performed by the User.
		</li>
		<li>
			If you suspect your account has been compromised, change the password immediately: doing
			so revokes all active sessions on all devices.
		</li>
		<li>
			The email address is used for service messages: address confirmation, password
			recovery, and notifications about changes to these terms. The service does not send
			marketing emails.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>6. User Data and Content</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>
			Entries, wine cards, notes, and photos remain yours. By using the service, the User
			grants the Rightholder a worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free license to host, store,
			process, and display this content solely to the extent technically necessary to operate
			the service, include it in your export, and display it in a publication you created.
		</li>
		<li>
			The User confirms and warrants that they are entitled to upload these photos and texts
			and that these do not infringe the intellectual property or privacy rights of third
			parties.
		</li>
		<li>
			It is strictly prohibited to upload other people's personal data, unlawful materials,
			abusive content, or advertising.
		</li>
		<li>
			Store names enter a shared directory and become available to other Users when selecting
			a store; the link between a name and its author is not shown in the interface and is
			erased together with the account.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>7. Publishing an Entry via a Link</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>
			A link is created only by the User's explicit action. The address consists of 16 random
			characters and cannot be found by brute force.
		</li>
		<li>
			The publication includes photos, the wine and its characteristics, the rating, taste
			category, impressions, and notes, as well as the User's name — only if enabled in the
			settings. Price, store, email address, and other entries are not included.
		</li>
		<li>
			The link can be revoked in one click, after which the page stops opening. Copies,
			screenshots, and messenger caches made while the link was active are outside the
			Rightholder's control and responsibility.
		</li>
		<li>A published page is closed to indexing by search engines.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>8. Usage Restrictions</h2>
	<p>
		The following actions are strictly prohibited: interfering with the operation of the
		service, bypassing rate limits, collecting data by automated means (scraping), attempting
		to gain unauthorized access to other users' diaries, probing security vulnerabilities
		without the Rightholder's written permission, and using the service for unlawful purposes
		or to promote alcoholic beverages.
	</p>

	<h2>9. Disclaimer of Warranties</h2>
	<p>
		The service is provided on an "AS IS" and "AS AVAILABLE" basis. The Rightholder explicitly
		disclaims all warranties, whether express or implied, including fitness for a particular
		purpose. The Rightholder does not guarantee uninterrupted operation or the absence of
		errors: scheduled maintenance, updates, and outages caused by providers are possible.
		Database backups are made regularly; nevertheless, the User is strongly advised to keep
		their own export — it is available in the settings in CSV and JSON formats at any time.
	</p>

	<h2>10. Limitation of Liability</h2>
	<p>
		The service is a personal record-keeping tool, not medical, dietary, or other professional
		advice. Decisions about alcohol consumption are made by the User independently and at
		their own responsibility. To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, the
		Rightholder shall not be liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or
		punitive damages, or any loss of profits or revenues, arising out of the use of or
		inability to use the service.
	</p>

	<h2>11. Termination</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>
			The User may delete their account in the settings at any time. Deletion is soft: for 30
			days recovery upon request remains possible, after which the data is deleted
			irreversibly.
		</li>
		<li>
			The Rightholder reserves the right to suspend or terminate access in the event of a
			breach of these terms, a false date of birth, a threat to the operability or security of
			the service, or as required by law, where possible with prior notice by email.
		</li>
		<li>
			If the service is discontinued entirely, the Rightholder will notify Users at least 30
			days in advance and will keep data export available until that date.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>12. Changes to the Terms</h2>
	<p>
		A new version is published on this page with an updated date and version number. The
		Rightholder notifies Users of material changes at the email address provided during
		registration and, where necessary, requests consent again. Continued use of the service
		after a new version takes effect constitutes agreement with it.
	</p>

	<h2>13. Governing Law and Disputes</h2>
	<p>
		This agreement is governed by the laws of {field(VENUE.jurisdiction.en, 'governing law country')}.
		The parties resolve disputes by correspondence: a request is sent to
		{' '}<a href={`mailto:${OPERATOR.email}`}>{field(OPERATOR.email, 'contact email address')}</a>,
		with a response time of 30 days. Unresolved disputes shall be subject to the exclusive
		jurisdiction of {field(VENUE.disputeVenue.en, 'dispute venue')}.
	</p>

	<h2>14. Rightholder Details</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Name: {field(OPERATOR.name.en, 'operator name')}</li>
		<li>Registration: Tax ID {field(OPERATOR.registration, 'operator tax id')}</li>
		<li>Address: {field(OPERATOR.address.en, 'operator address')}</li>
		<li>
			Email: <a href={`mailto:${OPERATOR.email}`}>{field(OPERATOR.email, 'contact email address')}</a>
		</li>
	</ul>
</Page>
